{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522802-what-level-of-life-to-increase-mental-stats","id":1522802,"title":"What level of Life to increase mental stats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-19T15:15:02-07:00","id":1522802,"title":"What level of Life to increase mental stats?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As the title says, what level of Life would be required to increase mental stats? Your brain is a biological thing, that can be improved, whether changing sugar usage, increasing quantity and quality of connections between neurons, copying brain distribution/sectioning from other people or animals, etc, it seems that brain processing power and speed should be under the capabilities of Life.<br /> <br /> Life should at least be able to improve raw Intelligence and Wits (not sure about Resolve, lack of fear perhaps and extreme self assurance seem however something that Life could do).<br /> <br /> Is this possible, and at what level if so?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-19-2023, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T16:03:23-07:00","id":1522804,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t have Life directly buff/debuff Mental Attributes, not any more than Forces directly buffing/debuffing Physical Attributes. The mind is its own thing in Mage, not some arbitrary construct of brain chemistry. (That\u2019s why the Thyrsus have it as their Inferior Arcanum).<br /> <br /> However, just like how Forces spells can buff Physical <i>actions</i>, I\u2019d encourage Life spell that buff certain Mental actions\u2026\u2026 Maybe as a Reach option for Life 2 Body Control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T19:43:10-07:00","id":1522813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522802-what-level-of-life-to-increase-mental-stats?p=1522804#post1522804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t have Life directly buff/debuff Mental Attributes, not any more than Forces directly buffing/debuffing Physical Attributes. The mind is its own thing in Mage, not some arbitrary construct of brain chemistry. (That\u2019s why the Thyrsus have it as their Inferior Arcanum).<br /> <br /> However, just like how Forces spells can buff Physical <i>actions</i>, I\u2019d encourage Life spell that buff certain Mental actions\u2026\u2026 Maybe as a Reach option for Life 2 Body Control?</div> </div> </div> </div>^that.<br /> <br /> Even if we put aside that the mind is it's own territory where the Supernal is concerned, realistically, Resolve wouldn't be affected by whatever's done to the brain and nervous system and Intelligence has limitations from what can be done in terms of the raw machinations of the brain, particularly since the Attribute is presented in terms of raw knowledge and memory(and even the part of it that's defined by the capacity to solve difficult problems[with any due speed, since I assume we're not just wanting to let someone work out a problem on a non-temporally concerned scale] still often relies on how regularly one trains their brain to look for solutions in a variety of different ways and with a number of different semiotic tricks to facilitate the flexibility of thought). Wits is probably the only attribute that you can make a case for raw life improvement to have a direct correlation, since everything that Wits is is pretty easy to understand in terms of increased awareness through improvements to the sense organs, nerves transmitting information, and the brain processes it.<br /> <br /> Still, if you wanna go quick and dirty with and don't mind some of the imbalance that comes with it, I can also counter-argue myself on that point and on the basis of the original assumption that there's really no reason to assume you couldn't start affecting the Mental Attributes in about the same way you could physical ones with Life, and depending on your table, it's probably better on the whole for the fun to be had. I personally would not raid your house over it.<br /> <br /> But in terms of canon, what Hermit said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T14:36:04-07:00","id":1522857,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to make someone smarter with life magic, I'd take a step back and try to do it a bit indirectly. You could use Life magic to help someone sleep and exercise, cure any health issues they have, improve their nutrition, and maybe do some genetic engineering. That wouldn't instantly add dice to their academics roll, but small tweaks like that could definitely make someone noticeably smarter over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T18:42:02-07:00","id":1522869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522802-what-level-of-life-to-increase-mental-stats#post1522802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your brain is a biological thing, that can be improved, whether changing sugar usage, increasing quantity and quality of connections between neurons, copying brain distribution/sectioning from other people or animals, etc, it seems that brain processing power and speed should be under the capabilities of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that, strictly speaking, some of these things can be targeted by Life spells, and achieving the end results of each of them would mostly be a matter of Perfecting and Weaving spells, even a few Rulings.<br /> <br /> &quot;Each of them&quot; being the operative term.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is not operating at the level of resolution where it engages with a subject in terms of the finer mechanical intricacies of its phenomenal existence. It deals with Patterns, the collection of Forms and Symbols that composes the abstraction of a subject's being. <br /> <br /> Spells do not achieve effects by handling all of the tricky, fiddly elements of the physical quality, they invoke the symbolism, verging on mythology, that says a thing works a certain way, and for the duration it does, overriding Phenomenal concerns. That's why a Forces spell for flight doesn't need to worry about aerodynamics or gravitation. It's why pretty much everything dealing with the Space Arcanum doesn't describe the topic in terms of the dimensional fabric of reality so much as &quot;things are as distant from one another as they feel&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think that a mage could cast individual spells that each target specific qualities of how a person's metabolism is functioning and the meat of which they are composed to make a number of fine connections that they know collectively come together to result in a higher functioning brain that translates to certain Mental stats. It's a lot of effort and a number of points on spell control, and I'd say some of the spells involved might require heavy Reach to cover those effects, but could be done.<br /> <br /> One just needs to be willing to fiddle around, step by step, inside of a person's most vital organ to recalibrate its key functions, in accordance with principles that are still only partially understood.<br /> <br /> How many test subjects does one need before they know the level of modification that results in a superior brain rather than a vegetable? That's a question for people of lesser will and greater Wisdom to worry about.<br /> <br /> The moral of the story is, no you can't reference subatomic physics to justify that sick thing you want to do with Forces.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}